vzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-17T21:53:49Z","updated_at":"2024-11-17T21:53:49Z","body":"Min. size was selected to ensure all UI elements fit and are usable, simply changing it won't work.\r\n\r\nIt's more an issue with a GNOME than with Godot, for example macOS tiling and side-by-side full-screen handle it without issues and simply fill more than a half of the screen when doing it on a small screen.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2481610431/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2481631735","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99369#issuecomment-2481631735","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99369","id":2481631735,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6T6rH3","user":{"login":"tetrapod00","id":145553014,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKz2dg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145553014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00","html_url":"https://github.com/tetrapod00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-17T22:21:40Z","updated_at":"2024-11-17T22:25:45Z","body":"See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7156, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/84114, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/95681, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/97878.\r\nAs far as I know, the main things contributing to a large minimum horizontal width are the *bottom panel* and the *workspace toolbar*. If both of those can be changed to require a smaller minimum width, then I believe the Godot editor can have a minimum width of less than 960 pixels.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2481631735/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2481635551","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99369#issuecomment-2481635551","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99369","id":2481635551,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6T6sDf","user":{"login":"musjj","id":72612857,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNjEyODU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72612857?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/musjj","html_url":"https://github.com/musjj","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/musjj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/musjj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/musjj/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/musjj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/musjj/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/musjj/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/musjj/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/musjj/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/musjj/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-17T22:29:40Z","updated_at":"2024-11-17T22:29:40Z","body":"> Min. size was selected to ensure all UI elements fit and are usable,\r\n\r\nI understand, but the min size is still too big IMO. Blender's window can be as small as 320x240 and it works just fine. And Blender's UI is as complex (or more) as Godot.\r\n\r\nI also tested other applications like Chrome, Firefox, Visual Studio Code and they all are just as resizable.\r\n\r\n> See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7156, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/84114, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/95681, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/97878.\r\n\r\nThanks for the links! Glad that there are people working on this.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2481635551/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3413563635","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99369#issuecomment-3413563635","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99369","id":3413563635,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ldtjz","user":{"login":"brainrot-coder-3000","id":238155824,"node_id":"U_kgDODjH4MA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238155824?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brainrot-coder-3000","html_url":"https://github.com/brainrot-coder-3000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brainrot-coder-3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brainrot-coder-3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brainrot-coder-3000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brainrot-coder-3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brainrot-coder-3000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brainrot-coder-3000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brainrot-coder-3000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brainrot-coder-3000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brainrot-coder-3000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T02:44:49Z","updated_at":"2025-10-17T09:58:45Z","body":"my only solution to this is to:\nEditor settings -> Interface -> Editor -> Custom display scale: set to 75%\nMain & Code Font size set to 17\n\nthe text is blurry, but i can't live without window side-by-side tiling. i like to easily look up the reference while im doing godot dev stuff. This is not gnome issue, this is the same with xfce, cinnamon, and windows 11 as i tried.\n\ngodot minimum width should NOT be higher than half of 1080p width (which is 540px height and 960px width), especially considering that its most popular of monitor resolution","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":